      "content": "Defenders of the Electoral College argue it protects the interests of smaller states, preventing candidates from focusing solely on large population centers. They maintain that it forces candidates to build broad, geographically diverse coalitions across the entire nation, not just in a few urban hubs. Furthermore, proponents claim it ensures the President has a mandate derived from a nationwide distribution of support, rather than just a plurality in densely populated areas. This structure, they argue, preserves the federal nature of the United States.",
