      "content": "i hear that, but it feels like those arguments are kind of outdated or just used to justify a flawed system. like, the \"protecting small states\" thing feels like a stretch when most of the power still stays in just a few swing states anyway. do you think there's actually any logical way to defend it in a modern democracy, or is it basically just a relic that's doing more harm than good at this point?",
